      "budget_share": 0.6,
      "why": "The spec requires 32 results/us (32 Msps) with a 0.44 us p99 batch deadline. A 1-result/cycle pipelined design is the only way to hit 32 Msps at a reasonable Fmax, but I am restricted to iterative/unrolled_k. unrolled_k with k=4..8 can reach 32 Msps if Fmax >= 4..8 MHz, which is trivially met. The batch of 32 requests must complete in 0.44 us; with k=8 and N=16, latency is ceil(16/8)+3 = 5 cycles, and 32 sequential requests take 32*ceil(16/8) = 64 cycles. At Fmax ~200 MHz that is 0.32 us, well under 0.44 us. k=4 gives 32*4=128 cycles ~0.64 us at 200 MHz, too slow. So k must be high (6-8) to meet the batch deadline. data_width 14-18 and n_iter 12-18 cover the accuracy requirement (max_abs_err <= 2^-12 = 0.000244). Lower data_width/n_iter minimises area."
    },
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 14,
          "high": 18
